# Committed (not secret) - a build-mode-specific CSP tuning knob, not a per-developer value.
# Vite auto-loads this file only for `vite`/`npm run dev`, never for `vite build` (see
# .env.production, its exact opposite).
#
# Vite's dev server injects live CSS as an inline <style> tag (for instant HMR updates,
# instead of a real stylesheet file) - confirmed by a real, reproduced bug: with a strict
# style-src, the browser console showed "Applying inline style violates ... style-src 'self'"
# and every button/card on the page rendered with default unstyled browser chrome
# (getComputedStyle confirmed backgroundColor was still the browser default, not any CSS from
# global.css). 'unsafe-inline' is scoped to dev-only for exactly this reason - see
# index.html's own comment for why production doesn't need it at all.
VITE_CSP_STYLE_SRC="'self' 'unsafe-inline'"
